    <bpmn:process id="W_W488" name="W488. Credit Card Chargeback Dispute Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Chargeback notification from acquiring bank or card processor
Frequency: ~150–250 chargebacks/month (estimated ~0.015–0.025% of ~1M monthly card transactions)
Volume: ~150–250 disputes/month; average chargeback value: PHP 3,000–8,000
Owner: Finance — Payment Settlement Specialist
Participants: Store Manager, Cashier, LP Analyst, Customer Service, Card Processor/Acquiring Bank
Source: workflow W488 — Credit Card Chargeback Dispute Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W488_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W488_Lane1" name="Payment Settlement Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W488_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W488_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W488_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W488_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W488_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W488_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W488_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W488_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W488_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W488_Start3" name="Chargeback notification from acquiring bank or card processor">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W488_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W488_Task4" name="Chargeback Notification Receipt">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Chargeback Notification Receipt: Payment Settlement Specialist receives chargeback notification from acquiring bank (BDO, BPI, or processor): (a) chargeback case number, card network (Visa/MC/JCB), reason code, transaction date, transaction amount, cardholder claim; (b) acquiring bank debits BuildRight&#x27;s settlement account for the chargeback amount (provisional debit); (c) log chargeback in chargeback tracking system with response deadline
Responsible (R): Payment Settlement Specialist
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W488_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W488_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W488_Task5" name="Transaction Investigation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Transaction Investigation: Payment Settlement Specialist pulls transaction details: (a) POS transaction record (transaction number, store, terminal ID, cashier ID, date/time, items purchased, amount); (b) signed/EMV chip card receipt or contactless payment confirmation; (c) CCTV footage if fraud alleged (via W71 — coordinate with store security); (d) customer lookup in loyalty system if card is linked to loyalty account; (e) check for related return/exchange records (W12A/W12B) if credit-not-processed claim
Responsible (R): Payment Settlement Specialist
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W488_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W488_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W488_Task6" name="Chargeback Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Chargeback Assessment: Payment Settlement Specialist determines response strategy: (a) Accept: if investigation confirms legitimate chargeback (e.g., proven duplicate charge, unauthorized use with no EMV/chip read); (b) Represent (Fight): if evidence supports that transaction was legitimate (e.g., EMV chip read, signed receipt, CCTV shows cardholder, loyalty account match); (c) Partial Accept: for multi-item transactions where only some items are disputed
Responsible (R): Payment Settlement Specialist
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W488_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W488_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W488_Task7" name="Representment Package Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Representment Package Preparation: For chargebacks being contested, Payment Settlement Specialist compiles representment evidence: (a) transaction receipt (signed or EMV-verified); (b) POS system transaction detail; (c) delivery proof (for large items with home delivery W5D); (d) return/exchange history showing customer did not return the item; (e) loyalty account activity showing the cardholder&#x27;s typical purchasing pattern; (f) CCTV screenshot showing cardholder at POS (if available and permitted by data privacy W271); (g) any customer communication acknowledging the purchase; (h) compile into card network-specific representment format
Responsible (R): Payment Settlement Specialist
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 30–60 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W488_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W488_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W488_Task8" name="Representment Submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Representment Submission: Payment Settlement Specialist submits representment through acquiring bank&#x27;s chargeback portal: (a) upload evidence package before deadline; (b) acquiring bank forwards to issuing bank; (c) issuing bank reviews and either: reverses the chargeback (BuildRight wins — credit back to account) or maintains the chargeback (cardholder wins); (d) complex cases may escalate to second chargeback or pre-arbitration
Responsible (R): Payment Settlement Specialist
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W488_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W488_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W488_Task9" name="Resolution &amp; Reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Resolution &amp; Reconciliation: Payment Settlement Specialist records the outcome: (a) Chargeback Reversed: credit received from acquiring bank; reconcile against original debit in settlement reconciliation (W99); (b) Chargeback Upheld: debit is finalized; write off as chargeback expense; no further action unless pattern detected; (c) Pre-Arbitration/Loss: for high-value disputes (&gt;PHP 50,000), escalate to Finance Manager for arbitration decision; arbitration fees may exceed disputed amount for smaller cases
Responsible (R): Payment Settlement Specialist
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W488_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W488_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W488_Task10" name="Pattern Analysis &amp; Prevention">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Pattern Analysis &amp; Prevention: Monthly, Payment Settlement Specialist analyzes chargeback trends: (a) chargeback rate by store, by reason code, by card network; (b) identify stores exceeding the internal 0.05% early-warning threshold (network monitoring programs trigger at 0.75–1.0%); (c) identify recurring fraud patterns (specific SKUs, specific terminal, specific cashier); (d) recommend preventive actions: enhanced cashier training (W51), terminal EMV enforcement, fraud alert rules; (e) escalate suspicious patterns to LP (W37, W466); (f) report chargeback metrics in monthly payment settlement reconciliation report (W99)
Responsible (R): Payment Settlement Specialist
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W488_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W488_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W488_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W488_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W488_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-285 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Payment &amp; Reconciliation (PA-15.2).) | - operational: Finance — Payment Settlement Specialist review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Finance — Payment Settlement Specialist</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W488_Assoc13" sourceRef="W488_Annotation12" targetRef="W488_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
