    <bpmn:process id="W_W489" name="W489. Store-Level Operating Budget &amp; Cost Control" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual budget preparation cycle (W26); monthly cost review; mid-year budget revision
Frequency: Annual (budget creation); monthly (actual vs. budget review); quarterly (forecast update)
Volume: 200 stores + 4 DCs; each location has an operating budget
Owner: Finance — FP&amp;A Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Regional Manager, VP Store Operations, Controller, CFO, DC Manager
Source: workflow W489 — Store-Level Operating Budget &amp; Cost Control</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W489_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W489_Lane1" name="FP&amp;A Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W489_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W489_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W489_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W489_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W489_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W489_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W489_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W489_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W489_Lane3" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W489_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W489_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W489_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W489_Start5" name="Annual budget preparation cycle (W26); monthly cost review; mid-year budget revision">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W489_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W489_Task6" name="Budget Template Distribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Budget Template Distribution: FP&amp;A Manager distributes store-level budget templates to Regional Managers: (a) template includes: revenue targets (top-down from W26), cost categories (payroll, utilities, maintenance, supplies, security, shrinkage provision), and capital requests (minor store improvements &lt; PHP 500K); (b) templates are pre-populated with prior-year actuals and known cost drivers (e.g., minimum wage increase per region, utility rate changes); (c) each Regional Manager cascades to their ~40 Store Managers
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W489_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W489_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W489_Task7" name="Store Manager Budget Input">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store Manager Budget Input: Store Manager reviews template and provides input: (a) validate revenue target against local market conditions (construction activity in area, competitor presence); (b) estimate labor hours needed based on sales forecast and shift schedule (W34); (c) flag known upcoming costs (lease escalation per W117, planned maintenance per W47, security upgrade); (d) submit minor capital requests with justification; (e) submit budget to Regional Manager for review
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–3 days/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W489_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W489_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W489_Task8" name="Regional Consolidation &amp; Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Regional Consolidation &amp; Review: Regional Manager reviews budgets for their ~40 stores: (a) verify reasonableness of cost assumptions (labor ratios, utility benchmarks per sqm); (b) identify outliers (stores with cost growth exceeding revenue growth); (c) resolve conflicts between stores competing for shared resources; (d) consolidate regional budget and submit to FP&amp;A
Responsible (R): Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 week/region</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W489_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W489_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W489_Task9" name="FP&amp;A Consolidation &amp; Approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: FP&amp;A Consolidation &amp; Approval: FP&amp;A consolidates all 200 store and 4 DC operating budgets: (a) verify total store-level costs align with enterprise budget (W26); (b) identify stores requiring cost reduction targets; (c) approve or adjust individual store budgets; (d) obtain CFO approval for final store-level budgets; (e) load approved budgets into ERP budget module by cost center per location
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W489_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W489_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W489_Task10" name="Monthly Cost Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly Cost Review: Store Manager reviews monthly actual vs. budget: (a) FP&amp;A generates store-level variance report (actual vs. budget by cost category); (b) Store Manager reviews and provides explanations for material variances (&gt;5% or &gt;PHP 50K); (c) identify cost overruns requiring corrective action; (d) submit variance explanations to Regional Manager
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours/store/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W489_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W489_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W489_Task11" name="Cost Control Action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Cost Control Action: For stores with material budget overruns: (a) Regional Manager and Store Manager agree on corrective actions: reduce overtime (W34 scheduling adjustment), renegotiate local service contracts (W47 maintenance), implement utility conservation measures (W111), tighten shrinkage controls (W248, W466); (b) corrective actions documented with target completion dates; (c) FP&amp;A tracks corrective action implementation in monthly review
Responsible (R): Regional Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–2 days/store/issue</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W489_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W489_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W489_Task12" name="Quarterly Forecast Update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quarterly Forecast Update: Each quarter, FP&amp;A updates store-level forecasts: (a) adjust revenue forecasts based on actual performance; (b) update cost forecasts for known changes (new minimum wage rates, utility rate adjustments, lease escalations); (c) identify stores at risk of missing annual budget; (d) recommend mid-year corrective actions (cost reduction, schedule optimization, store closure evaluation per W45); (e) update enterprise forecast (W26) with consolidated store-level revisions
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 week/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W489_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W489_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W489_Task13" name="Annual Performance Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Annual Performance Assessment: At year-end, FP&amp;A prepares store-level budget performance summary: (a) actual vs. budget by store (revenue, gross margin, controllable expenses, store contribution margin); (b) rank stores by performance; (c) identify top-performing and bottom-performing stores; (d) feed into Store Manager performance review (W72) and monthly store performance review (W67); (e) inform next year&#x27;s budget template with updated benchmarks
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks/annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W489_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W489_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W489_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W489_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W489_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-285 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Payment &amp; Reconciliation (PA-15.2).) | - operational: Finance — FP&amp;A Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Finance — FP&amp;A Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
