    <bpmn:process id="W_W556" name="W556. AP Payment Run &amp; Batch Processing Execution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly/biweekly payment schedule (e.g., every Friday and last business day of month); ad-hoc urgent payments
Frequency: 2 scheduled payment runs per week; ~1 ad-hoc urgent run per week
Volume: ~800–1,200 vendor payments per scheduled run; total monthly AP payments ~8,000–10,000 (matching the ~8,500–9,500 monthly invoice inflow)
Owner: AP Supervisor / Treasury Analyst
Participants: AP Specialist, AP Supervisor, Treasury Analyst (R for cash positioning), Finance Manager (A for large payments &gt; PHP 1M), Bank (payment execution)
Source: workflow W556 — AP Payment Run &amp; Batch Processing Execution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W556_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W556_Lane1" name="AP Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W556_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W556_Lane3" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W556_Lane4" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W556_Lane5" name="AP Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task20</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_Task21</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W556_End22</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W556_Start7" name="Weekly/biweekly payment schedule (e.g., every Friday and last business day of month)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W556_Task8" name="AP Supervisor initiates payment run in ERP: selects payment date, payment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AP Supervisor initiates payment run in ERP: selects payment date, payment method filters (bank transfer, PESONet, check), vendor grouping options (by vendor, by due date, by payment terms); system presents payment proposal screen with all eligible invoices
Responsible (R): AP Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/run</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W556_Task9" name="System auto-selects invoices meeting payment criteria: (a) due date within…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System auto-selects invoices meeting payment criteria: (a) due date within payment window (payment date ± 5 business days); (b) fully approved per W7 workflow (no pending approvals); (c) not on payment hold or dispute per W244; (d) vendor bank details validated and active; system calculates total payment proposal amount and displays summary by payment method
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W556_Task10" name="System applies payment term optimization: (a) early payment discount capture —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System applies payment term optimization: (a) early payment discount capture — invoices eligible for discount per W324 (dynamic discounting) are flagged with discount amount, discount deadline, and annualized ROI; (b) net due date calculation per W295 (payment terms master) — system groups invoices by payment term category; (c) discount priority ranking: discount invoices sorted by annualized ROI descending
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W556_Task11" name="Treasury Analyst reviews proposed payment total against cash position per W30…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Treasury Analyst reviews proposed payment total against cash position per W30: (a) total payment proposal amount vs. available bank balances; (b) upcoming cash inflows (AR collections, credit card settlements) vs. other cash outflows (payroll per W10, tax payments per W90, capex per W21); (c) FX payment requirements for import vendors (USD account balance); Treasury Analyst confirms sufficient liquidity or recommends payment prioritization
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 30 min/run</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W556_Task12" name="If cash shortfall identified: Treasury Analyst recommends payment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: If cash shortfall identified: Treasury Analyst recommends payment prioritization to AP Supervisor — (a) Tier 1: critical vendors (utilities, rent, tax, single-source suppliers) and discount opportunity invoices; (b) Tier 2: standard-term vendors within due date window; (c) Tier 3: vendors with extended terms (Net 60, Net 90) that can be deferred to next run; AP Supervisor adjusts payment proposal accordingly
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / AP Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 30 min/run (if shortfall)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W556_Task13" name="AP Supervisor adjusts payment proposal: add/remove individual invoices, split…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: AP Supervisor adjusts payment proposal: add/remove individual invoices, split payments across payment dates, apply partial payments for disputed invoices (pro-rata per W244 resolution), override payment method for specific vendors; system recalculates totals after each adjustment
Responsible (R): AP Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–30 min/run</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W556_Task14" name="AP Supervisor submits final payment proposal for approval; system generates…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: AP Supervisor submits final payment proposal for approval; system generates payment batch summary: total amount, number of invoices, number of vendors, payment method breakdown, discount capture summary
Responsible (R): AP Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/run</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W556_Task15" name="Finance Manager reviews and approves payment batch: (a) mandatory approval for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Finance Manager reviews and approves payment batch: (a) mandatory approval for batch totals &gt; PHP 10M or individual payments &gt; PHP 1M; (b) reviews discount capture opportunities accepted/rejected; (c) verifies cash position concurrence from Treasury Analyst; (d) approves or returns batch with comments for adjustment
Responsible (R): Finance Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15–30 min/run</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W556_Task16" name="System generates payment files per bank format requirements: (a) BDO — PESONet…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: System generates payment files per bank format requirements: (a) BDO — PESONet batch file format (XML); (b) BPI — PESONet batch file format (CSV); (c) Metrobank — PESONet batch file format (specific template); (d) Chinabank — PESONet batch file format; (e) check run — generates check printing file with MICR line data; system validates file format against bank schema before generation
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W556_Task17" name="AP Specialist transmits payment files to banks via secure channel per W320…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: AP Specialist transmits payment files to banks via secure channel per W320 (electronic banking security): (a) PESONet files uploaded to each bank&#x27;s corporate banking portal; (b) transmission confirmation receipt captured and filed; (c) for check payments: print checks on pre-numbered security stock per W317; (d) verify PESONet batch acceptance/rejection status within 2 hours of submission
Responsible (R): AP Specialist
Accountable (A): AP Supervisor
Duration: 30–45 min/run</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow35</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W556_Task18" name="For check payments: AP Specialist prints checks, obtains dual signatures per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: For check payments: AP Specialist prints checks, obtains dual signatures per W317 signatory management (signatory A: Finance Manager or above; signatory B: Controller or CFO — both required for amounts &gt; PHP 500K); mails or arranges courier delivery per vendor instructions; tracks check delivery confirmation
Responsible (R): AP Specialist
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/run (if checks included)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow35</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow36</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W556_Task19" name="System posts payment transactions: (a) clears AP invoices — Dr. Accounts…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: System posts payment transactions: (a) clears AP invoices — Dr. Accounts Payable / Cr. Bank (or Cash in Transit for PESONet pending); (b) updates vendor balances; (c) updates cash position per W30; (d) captures early payment discounts taken — Dr. Accounts Payable / Cr. Purchase Discount; (e) generates payment confirmation report with check numbers or PESONet reference numbers
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow36</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow37</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W556_Task20" name="Payment confirmation reconciliation: within 2 business days, AP Specialist…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 13: Payment confirmation reconciliation: within 2 business days, AP Specialist matches bank debit advices against payment batch — (a) PESONet: verify batch settlement amount matches payment total; (b) checks: verify cleared checks against issued check register; (c) discrepancies investigated and resolved per W89 bank reconciliation; (d) uncleared checks &gt; 30 days flagged for follow-up
Responsible (R): AP Specialist
Accountable (A): AP Supervisor
Duration: 30 min/run</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow37</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow38</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W556_Task21" name="Exception handling: (a) returned payments (wrong account number, closed…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 14: Exception handling: (a) returned payments (wrong account number, closed account) — AP Specialist contacts vendor for corrected bank details, reprocesses payment in next run; (b) rejected PESONet files — correct file format errors per bank rejection reason, resubmit same day; (c) stale-dated checks (uncashed after 6 months per Philippine law) — escheatment processing: notify vendor, if unclaimed after the statutory holding period, escheat to the Bureau of the Treasury per Act No. 3936 (Unclaimed Balances Law)
Responsible (R): AP Specialist / AP Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/month (exception handling)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow38</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W556_Flow39</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W556_End22" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W556_Flow39</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W556_Annotation23">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-285 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Payment &amp; Reconciliation (PA-15.2).) | - operational: ERP bank format templates and pre-submission validation; operational: alternate signatory delegation per W317 and electronic payment migration for repeat vendors; operational: system auto-exclusion of invoices with active dispute status
Owner: AP Supervisor / Treasury Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W556_Assoc24" sourceRef="W556_Annotation23" targetRef="W556_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
