    <bpmn:process id="W_W611" name="W611. Payment Gateway Daily Operations &amp; Settlement Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Start of business day; continuous throughout operating hours
Frequency: Daily
Volume: ~2.8M POS transactions/month; ~42,900 ecommerce orders/month; ~36% card, ~15% e-wallet
Owner: Treasury Analyst
Participants: Treasury Analyst, IT Integration Specialist, POS Administrator, Finance Analyst
Source: workflow W611 — Payment Gateway Daily Operations &amp; Settlement Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W611_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W611_Lane1" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W611_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W611_Lane3" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W611_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W611_Start5" name="Start of business day; continuous throughout operating hours">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W611_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W611_Task6" name="Morning: Treasury Analyst reviews payment gateway health dashboard —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Morning: Treasury Analyst reviews payment gateway health dashboard — connectivity status for all active gateways (card acquirer, PayMongo, Dragonpay, GCash, Maya), transaction success rate (target ≥ 99.5%), average response time, and any overnight settlement files received
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W611_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W611_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W611_Task7" name="System auto-processes overnight settlement files: card acquirer settlement file…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System auto-processes overnight settlement files: card acquirer settlement file (previous day&#x27;s batch close per W537), e-wallet settlement files (GCash, Maya, GrabPay — T+1 settlement), ecommerce payment gateway settlement (PayMongo, Dragonpay — T+1 to T+2)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W611_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W611_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W611_Task8" name="Treasury Analyst reviews auto-matching results: settlement amount vs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Treasury Analyst reviews auto-matching results: settlement amount vs. POS/ecommerce recorded transactions; system flags unmatched items (missing transactions, amount discrepancies, MDR fee variance &gt; 0.1%)
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W611_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W611_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W611_Task9" name="For unmatched items: Treasury Analyst investigates — (a) timing differences…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: For unmatched items: Treasury Analyst investigates — (a) timing differences (settlement file covers different cutoff than POS batch close), (b) MDR rate discrepancy (new rate not configured), (c) failed transactions not captured, (d) duplicate settlement entries
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W611_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W611_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W611_Task10" name="If MDR rate discrepancy: Treasury Analyst creates configuration change request…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: If MDR rate discrepancy: Treasury Analyst creates configuration change request to POS Administrator for rate update in payment gateway master; verifies contracted rate vs. billed rate
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): POS Administrator
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W611_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W611_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W611_Task11" name="Mid-day: system monitors real-time payment gateway transaction success rate; if…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Mid-day: system monitors real-time payment gateway transaction success rate; if success rate drops below 98%, auto-alerts IT Integration Specialist and Treasury Analyst for immediate investigation (connectivity issue, gateway outage, API rate limiting)
Responsible (R): System / IT Specialist
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: As needed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W611_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W611_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W611_Task12" name="End of day: Treasury Analyst reviews daily settlement reconciliation summary —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: End of day: Treasury Analyst reviews daily settlement reconciliation summary — total processed, matched, unmatched, and aging of unresolved items; unresolved items &gt; 5 business days escalated to Controller
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W611_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W611_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W611_Task13" name="Weekly: Treasury Analyst generates payment gateway performance report —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Weekly: Treasury Analyst generates payment gateway performance report — transaction volumes by gateway, success rates, settlement timeliness, MDR costs, chargeback rates (per W488); presents to Finance Manager
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W611_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W611_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W611_Task14" name="Monthly: Finance Manager reviews total payment processing costs (MDR, gateway…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Monthly: Finance Manager reviews total payment processing costs (MDR, gateway fees, chargeback losses) vs. budget; evaluates new payment method requests (e.g., new e-wallet, BNPL provider); coordinates onboarding with IT Integration Specialist
Responsible (R): Finance Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W611_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W611_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W611_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W611_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W611_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-285 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Payment &amp; Reconciliation (PA-15.2).) | - operational: multi-gateway redundancy and automatic failover; operational: failover; operational: automated matching and tolerance-based auto-reconciliation
Owner: Treasury Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W611_Assoc17" sourceRef="W611_Annotation16" targetRef="W611_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
