    <bpmn:process id="W_W613" name="W613. Store-Level Weekly Payroll Accrual &amp; Labor Cost Flash Report" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: End of each work week (Sunday); semi-monthly cutoff dates (15th and 30th)
Frequency: Weekly flash; semi-monthly reconciliation
Volume: 200 stores; ~5,800 store employees; semi-monthly payroll of ~PHP 90M
Owner: Finance Analyst (Payroll)
Participants: Finance Analyst, Payroll Officer, Controller, Store Managers
Source: workflow W613 — Store-Level Weekly Payroll Accrual &amp; Labor Cost Flash Report</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W613_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W613_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W613_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W613_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W613_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W613_Lane2" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W613_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W613_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W613_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W613_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W613_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W613_Lane3" name="Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W613_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W613_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W613_Start5" name="End of each work week (Sunday); semi-monthly cutoff dates (15th and 30th)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W613_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W613_Task6" name="System accumulates daily payroll data from attendance system: regular hours…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System accumulates daily payroll data from attendance system: regular hours, overtime hours (with premium), holiday hours, night differential hours, leave hours — per employee per store
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W613_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W613_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W613_Task7" name="Weekly (Monday): Finance Analyst runs weekly payroll accrual flash report for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Weekly (Monday): Finance Analyst runs weekly payroll accrual flash report for all 200 stores — estimated gross payroll by store based on hours worked × applicable rates; includes overtime, holiday, night differential, and projected statutory deductions
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W613_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W613_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W613_Task8" name="Finance Analyst compares weekly flash to pro-rated weekly payroll budget…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Finance Analyst compares weekly flash to pro-rated weekly payroll budget (monthly budget ÷ 4.33); flags stores exceeding weekly budget by &gt; 10%; investigates causes (overtime surge, holiday week, new hires)
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W613_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W613_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W613_Task9" name="System auto-generates GL accrual entry: DR Payroll Expense (by store cost…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System auto-generates GL accrual entry: DR Payroll Expense (by store cost center) / CR Accrued Payroll Liability; accrual based on hours worked to date × average hourly rate; adjusting entry posted at semi-monthly payroll actual (per W10)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W613_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W613_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W613_Task10" name="Semi-monthly (after payroll run per W10): Finance Analyst reconciles accrued…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Semi-monthly (after payroll run per W10): Finance Analyst reconciles accrued payroll (from weekly flashes) to actual payroll posted; posts adjusting entry for variance (typically &lt; 3%); investigates variances &gt; 5% by store
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W613_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W613_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W613_Task11" name="Finance Analyst distributes weekly flash to Store Managers via mobile…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Finance Analyst distributes weekly flash to Store Managers via mobile dashboard: their store&#x27;s week-to-date labor cost, budget comparison, and department breakdown; Store Managers use for overtime decisions (per W602)
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W613_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W613_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W613_Task12" name="Monthly: Controller reviews payroll accrual accuracy — compares total accrued…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly: Controller reviews payroll accrual accuracy — compares total accrued vs. actual for trailing 3 months; adjusts accrual methodology if systematic bias detected (consistent over/under accrual)
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W613_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W613_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W613_Task13" name="Quarterly: Finance Analyst prepares labor cost trend analysis for CFO —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Quarterly: Finance Analyst prepares labor cost trend analysis for CFO — store-level labor cost as % of revenue trend, overtime trend, headcount efficiency (revenue per employee per store), seasonal pattern analysis
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W613_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W613_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W613_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W613_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W613_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-285 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Payment &amp; Reconciliation (PA-15.2).) | - operational: semi-monthly true-up in Step 5; operational: holiday calendar awareness and separate holiday accrual line item; operational: W366 network monitoring and offline attendance buffering
Owner: Finance Analyst (Payroll)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
