    <bpmn:process id="W_W713" name="W713. Corporate Credit Card Program Management &amp; Expense Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly corporate credit card statement receipt; or employee expense report submission
Frequency: Monthly (statement reconciliation); daily (transaction monitoring)
Volume: ~150–200 corporate cardholders; ~3,000–4,000 transactions/month; ~PHP 15-20M monthly spend
Owner: Finance Manager
Participants: Cardholder (Employee), Approving Manager, AP Clerk, Finance Manager, Bank
Source: workflow W713 — Corporate Credit Card Program Management &amp; Expense Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W713_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W713_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W713_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W713_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W713_Lane2" name="AP Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W713_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W713_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W713_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W713_Lane3" name="Cardholder">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W713_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W713_Lane4" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W713_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W713_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W713_Start6" name="Monthly corporate credit card statement receipt; or employee expense report submission">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W713_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W713_Task7" name="Transaction monitoring (daily)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Transaction monitoring (daily): system imports corporate card transactions daily via bank feed per FIN-009: (a) automated transaction categorization based on merchant category code (MCC); (b) policy violation alerts: transactions exceeding per-transaction limit, restricted merchant categories (casinos, personal items), weekend/holiday transactions without travel approval; (c) fraud pattern detection: transactions in unusual locations, rapid sequential charges, split transactions to avoid limits; (d) alerts routed to cardholder&#x27;s approving manager for review
Responsible (R): System / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 30-60 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W713_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W713_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W713_Task8" name="Monthly statement reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly statement reconciliation: upon monthly statement receipt: (a) system matches card transactions to submitted expense reports (where applicable); (b) unmatched transactions flagged: cardholder must submit expense report within 5 business days; (c) system reconciles statement total vs. GL accrual for outstanding card transactions; (d) verify all transactions have supporting receipts per retention policy W256; (e) bank charges, interest, and FX markups verified and coded
Responsible (R): AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 4-6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W713_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W713_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W713_Task9" name="Expense report review and approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Expense report review and approval: cardholder submits expense report per W74 process with corporate card charges pre-populated: (a) each line item requires: business purpose, cost center allocation, project code (if applicable), receipt attachment; (b) approving manager reviews for policy compliance: per-meal limits, hotel rate caps, airfare class restrictions; (c) exceptions require Finance Manager approval with justification; (d) approved expenses coded to correct GL accounts and cost centers
Responsible (R): Cardholder / Approving Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 10-15 min per report</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W713_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W713_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W713_Task10" name="Payment processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payment processing: (a) system generates corporate card payment file per W556; (b) full balance payment (no revolving credit on corporate cards); (c) payment funded from appropriate entity bank account based on cardholder&#x27;s employing entity; (d) split payment if cardholder&#x27;s expenses span multiple entities; (e) payment confirmed via bank statement reconciliation per W89
Responsible (R): AP Clerk / Finance Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1-2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W713_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W713_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W713_Task11" name="Card lifecycle management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Card lifecycle management: (a) new card issuance: employee request with manager approval → Finance Manager reviews credit limit request → bank application → card activation; (b) credit limit review: annual review of all cardholder limits based on role, travel frequency, and historical spend; (c) card suspension/cancellation: employee separation triggers immediate card suspension per W43 offboarding checklist; policy violations trigger temporary suspension; (d) lost/stolen card: 24-hour reporting requirement → bank hotline → emergency replacement
Responsible (R): AP Clerk / Finance Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W713_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W713_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W713_Task12" name="Quarterly program review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly program review: (a) spend analytics: total spend by category, department, entity, and cardholder; (b) policy compliance rate: % of transactions with timely expense reports, % with receipts, % of flagged transactions; (c) cost optimization: negotiate bank fee reductions based on volume, evaluate reward programs, assess card program vs. petty cash usage per W25; (d) fraud summary: confirmed fraud incidents, recovery rate, control improvements; (e) report to CFO with recommendations
Responsible (R): Finance Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4-6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W713_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W713_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W713_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W713_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W713_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-285 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Payment &amp; Reconciliation (PA-15.2).) | - operational: Finance Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Finance Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
