    <bpmn:process id="W_W769" name="W769. Customer Overpayment Detection &amp; Refund Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Automated detection during payment reconciliation; or customer inquiry
Frequency: Weekly review; daily automated detection
Volume: ~100–200 overpayments per month (~PHP 1-3M)
Owner: AR Accountant
Participants: AR Accountant, Finance Manager, Customer (B2B trade/corporate)
Source: workflow W769 — Customer Overpayment Detection &amp; Refund Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W769_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W769_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W769_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W769_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W769_Lane2" name="AR Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W769_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W769_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W769_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W769_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W769_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W769_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W769_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W769_Start4" name="Automated detection during payment reconciliation; or customer inquiry">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W769_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W769_Task5" name="Automated overpayment detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Automated overpayment detection: During daily payment reconciliation per W99 and cash application: system flags payments where: (a) payment amount exceeds invoice balance by &gt; PHP 100, (b) payment applied to already-paid invoice, (c) payment with no matching invoice (on-account payment)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W769_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W769_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W769_Task6" name="Overpayment classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Overpayment classification: AR Accountant reviews each flagged overpayment and classifies: (a) Duplicate payment — same invoice paid twice, (b) Misapplication — payment intended for different invoice, (c) Credit memo not applied — customer paid gross without deducting issued credit note per W766, (d) Genuine overpayment — customer paid more than owed
Responsible (R): AR Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5-10 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W769_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W769_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W769_Task7" name="Misapplication correction">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Misapplication correction: For misapplied payments: AR Accountant re-applies payment to correct invoice; no customer communication needed; system updates AR aging per W108
Responsible (R): AR Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W769_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W769_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W769_Task8" name="Customer notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer notification: For genuine overpayments and unapplied credits &gt; PHP 500: AR Accountant initiates customer notification per W708: (a) details of overpayment (invoice number, payment date, excess amount), (b) refund options: (i) credit note for future purchases per W101, (ii) wire transfer refund to original payment account, (iii) offset against other open invoices
Responsible (R): AR Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W769_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W769_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W769_Task9" name="Refund processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Refund processing: Based on customer preference: (a) Credit note: system generates credit note per W540 with BIR compliance, (b) Wire refund: AR Accountant prepares refund request per W101 approval matrix, Finance Manager approves, payment processed per W556, (c) Offset: system applies overpayment to customer&#x27;s oldest open invoice
Responsible (R): AR Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 10-15 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W769_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W769_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W769_Task10" name="Aging and escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Aging and escalation: Monthly: unresolved overpayments &gt; 60 days escalated: (a) second customer notification, (b) B2B accounts: Sales Manager outreach per W617 customer success, (c) overpayments &gt; 180 days assessed for breakage recognition per PFRS 15
Responsible (R): AR Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W769_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W769_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W769_Task11" name="Overpayment analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Overpayment analytics: Monthly: AR Accountant reports: (a) overpayment frequency by cause, (b) average resolution time, (c) total outstanding overpayment balance, (d) recurring customer patterns (indicating process improvement opportunity)
Responsible (R): AR Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W769_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W769_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W769_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W769_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W769_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-285 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Payment &amp; Reconciliation (PA-15.2).) | - operational: AR Accountant review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: AR Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W769_Assoc14" sourceRef="W769_Annotation13" targetRef="W769_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
