    <bpmn:process id="W_W814" name="W814. Credit Card Settlement Exception &amp; Chargeback Recovery Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Credit card acquirer issues chargeback notice or settlement discrepancy identified per W537/W99
Frequency: Weekly; ~150–250 chargebacks/month across 600 terminals (one register with W488)
Volume: ~80–120 chargebacks/month (~0.003% of 2.8M transactions); ~PHP 500K-1M disputed value/month
Owner: Finance Analyst (Payments)
Participants: Finance Analyst, Store Manager, Customer, Bank/Acquirer, Finance Manager
Source: workflow W814 — Credit Card Settlement Exception &amp; Chargeback Recovery Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W814_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W814_Lane1" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W814_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W814_Start3" name="Credit card acquirer issues chargeback notice or settlement discrepancy identified per…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W814_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W814_Task4" name="Chargeback notification receipt">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Chargeback notification receipt: Finance Analyst receives chargeback notification from acquiring bank via: (a) acquirer online merchant portal alert, (b) email notification from acquirer dispute resolution team, (c) debit advice from bank for chargebacks already deducted from settlement. Each notification includes: card scheme reason code, transaction date, transaction amount, card type, cardholder dispute reason, response deadline (typically 30 calendar days from notification date)
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5-10 min/notification</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W814_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W814_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W814_Task5" name="Transaction matching and initial assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Transaction matching and initial assessment: Finance Analyst matches chargeback to original POS transaction: (a) locate original transaction in POS system by: terminal ID, batch number, transaction reference, transaction date and time, and card last-4 digits, (b) verify transaction details: authorization code, settlement status, batch deposit date, (c) cross-reference with W537 settlement records to confirm transaction was included in batch deposit, (d) classify chargeback by reason code: (i) fraud (card not present, counterfeit card), (ii) authorization (declined authorization, no authorization obtained), (iii) processing error (duplicate charge, incorrect amount), (iv) cardholder dispute (product not received, product not as described, credit not processed), (v) friendly fraud (cardholder legitimately made purchase but disputes to avoid payment)
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10-15 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W814_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W814_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W814_Task6" name="Evidence compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Evidence compilation: Finance Analyst gathers representment evidence based on chargeback reason code: (a) for all chargebacks: (i) original signed or electronic receipt from POS terminal, (ii) POS transaction log showing authorization code and approval response, (iii) transaction detail from POS system including terminal ID, cashier ID, store location, (b) for &quot;product not received&quot; disputes: (i) goods receipt or delivery confirmation per W4 store delivery, (ii) signed delivery receipt or waybill, (iii) ecommerce tracking confirmation for online orders, (c) for &quot;product not as described&quot; disputes: (i) product listing/sales description at time of purchase, (ii) store display or online catalog screenshot, (iii) return policy documentation presented to customer, (d) for fraud disputes: (i) EMV chip read confirmation (if card-present), (ii) 3D Secure authentication result (if card-not-present/ecommerce), (iii) CCTV footage from store showing cardholder at POS (retention: 30 days per store policy; must request from Store Manager within 7 days), (iv) IP address and device fingerprint for ecommerce transactions per W519
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Store Manager (CCTV/evidence)
Duration: 20-40 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W814_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W814_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W814_Task7" name="Legitimate dispute — accept chargeback">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Legitimate dispute — accept chargeback: If Finance Analyst determines chargeback is legitimate: (a) customer was correctly charged twice for same transaction (duplicate), (b) customer returned product but refund not processed per W101, (c) transaction amount was incorrectly entered at POS, (d) Finance Analyst accepts chargeback in acquirer portal: system posts journal entry — Dr. Chargeback Expense (cost of doing business) / Cr. Bank (chargeback already deducted from settlement), (e) if root cause is store-level error: notify Store Manager for cashier training per W5B, (f) update chargeback tracker with acceptance reason
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W814_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W814_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W814_Task8" name="Contestable chargeback — compile representment package">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Contestable chargeback — compile representment package: If Finance Analyst determines chargeback is contestable (evidence supports that transaction was legitimate): (a) compile representment package per card scheme requirements: (i) cover letter summarizing dispute and evidence, (ii) copy of signed receipt or electronic signature capture, (iii) proof of delivery or service completion, (iv) authorization response documentation, (v) refund/return policy documentation, (vi) any prior correspondence with cardholder, (b) for Visa: submit via Visa Resolve Online (VROL) system or acquirer portal, (c) for Mastercard: submit via Mastercom or acquirer portal, (d) for JCB/UnionPay: submit through acquiring bank&#x27;s dispute channel, (e) submission must be completed within 30-day deadline — no extensions granted by card schemes
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30-60 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W814_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W814_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W814_Task9" name="Representment status tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Representment status tracking: Finance Analyst tracks representment through acquirer arbitration: (a) acquirer reviews representment package and submits to issuing bank, (b) issuing bank reviews and either: (i) accepts representment — chargeback reversed, funds returned to BuildRight&#x27;s settlement account, (ii) rejects representment — chargeback stands, (iii) escalates to second chargeback or pre-arbitration (Visa) / arbitration (Mastercard), (c) second chargeback/pre-arbitration: Finance Analyst evaluates whether to pursue further based on: (i) disputed amount, (ii) strength of additional evidence, (iii) arbitration filing fees (Visa: USD 500, Mastercard: USD 250-400), (d) update chargeback tracker with each status change and timeline
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager (&gt; PHP 50K)
Duration: 10-15 min/case/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W814_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W814_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W814_Task10" name="Representment outcome and root cause analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Representment outcome and root cause analysis: Upon final representment outcome: (a) if successful (chargeback reversed): system reverses chargeback entry — Dr. Bank / Cr. Chargeback Expense; confirm settlement deposit includes reversal amount in next batch per W537, (b) if unsuccessful (chargeback stands): chargeback remains as loss; Finance Analyst analyzes root cause: (i) was evidence sufficient? (ii) was deadline met? (iii) was store-level process deficient? (iv) is customer a repeat dispute filer (friendly fraud pattern)?, (c) update chargeback tracker with final outcome, root cause classification, and action items
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10-15 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W814_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W814_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W814_Task11" name="Monthly chargeback analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly chargeback analytics: Finance Analyst prepares monthly chargeback analytics report: (a) chargeback volume: total count and value vs. prior month and same month prior year, (b) chargeback rate: chargeback count / total card transaction count — must remain below 0.75% card scheme threshold, (c) breakdown by reason code: fraud, authorization, processing error, cardholder dispute, (d) breakdown by card type: Visa, Mastercard, JCB, UnionPay, (e) representment success rate: % of contested chargebacks successfully reversed, (f) top 10 stores by chargeback rate — identify stores needing cashier training or fraud prevention improvements, (g) top 10 stores by chargeback volume, (h) average chargeback value, (i) total chargeback expense (net of recoveries) vs. budget, (j) settlement exception count and value — batch discrepancies unresolved per W537, (k) present to Finance Manager with recommendations
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W814_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W814_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W814_Task12" name="Quarterly merchant fee analysis and cost optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Quarterly merchant fee analysis and cost optimization: Finance Analyst conducts quarterly review linked to W640 merchant fee analysis: (a) calculate effective MDR rate by card type and acquiring bank — actual MDR charges / card transaction volume, (b) compare MDR rates across BDO, BPI, Metrobank, EastWest — identify opportunities to renegotiate or consolidate acquiring relationships, (c) assess interchange fee category accuracy — ensure BuildRight is categorized correctly (retail / big-box vs. supermarket rates differ), (d) evaluate chargeback prevention ROI: cost of prevention measures (3D Secure, EMV, staff training) vs. chargeback losses avoided, (e) if chargeback rate exceeds 0.5%: implement enhanced prevention — mandatory chip-and-PIN for transactions above PHP 10K, enhanced ecommerce fraud screening per W519, (f) present analysis to Finance Manager for acquirer negotiation strategy
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W814_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W814_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W814_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W814_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W814_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-285 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Payment &amp; Reconciliation (PA-15.2).) | - operational: chargeback loss regardless of evidence strength
Owner: Finance Analyst (Payments)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W814_Assoc15" sourceRef="W814_Annotation14" targetRef="W814_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
