    <bpmn:process id="W_W1199" name="W1199. Import Letter of Credit (LC) Lifecycle, Amendment &amp; Bank Release Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Import purchase order confirmed with vendor requiring LC payment terms
Frequency: ~50–80 LC transactions/month (the PA-15.2 LC register per W1310; ~40% of import vendors requiring LC terms; remaining import vendors use TT/DP)
Volume: Average LC value: PHP 2M–10M per transaction; ~PHP 200M–400M in outstanding LCs at any time
Owner: Treasury Manager
Participants: Treasury Manager, Purchasing Manager, AP Clerk, Import Coordinator, Bank Relationship Manager, CFO (LC &gt; PHP 10M)
Source: workflow W1199 — Import Letter of Credit (LC) Lifecycle, Amendment &amp; Bank Release Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1199_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1199_Lane1" name="Purchasing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1199_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1199_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1199_Lane2" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1199_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1199_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1199_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1199_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1199_Lane3" name="Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1199_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1199_Lane4" name="Bank">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1199_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1199_Lane5" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1199_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1199_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1199_Start7" name="Import purchase order confirmed with vendor requiring LC payment terms">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1199_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1199_Task8" name="LC requirement determination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: LC requirement determination: At PO creation for import orders: system flags vendors with LC-required payment terms; Purchasing Manager confirms LC requirement and obtains CFO approval for LC &gt; PHP 10M; system creates LC request linked to import PO
Responsible (R): Purchasing Manager
Accountable (A): CFO (for &gt; PHP 10M)
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1199_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1199_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1199_Task9" name="LC application to bank">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: LC application to bank: Treasury Manager prepares LC application: (a) completes bank LC application form with PO details (vendor name, beneficiary bank, amount, currency, shipment date, Port of Loading, Port of Discharge), (b) attaches proforma invoice from vendor, (c) specifies LC terms: latest shipment date, document requirements (commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificate of origin, insurance certificate), (d) submits to bank (BDO/BPI/Metrobank — USD account); bank issues LC reference number
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1199_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1199_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1199_Task10" name="LC advice to vendor">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: LC advice to vendor: Bank transmits LC via SWIFT to vendor&#x27;s bank (advising bank); vendor&#x27;s bank advises vendor of LC terms; vendor confirms acceptance of LC terms or requests amendment; if amendment needed: Treasury Manager coordinates with Purchasing Manager and bank for LC amendment (extension of shipment date, quantity change, document waiver)
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Purchasing Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1199_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1199_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1199_Task11" name="Shipment and document presentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Shipment and document presentation: Vendor ships goods; prepares shipping documents per LC requirements; presents documents to their bank; documents transmitted to BuildRight&#x27;s bank via SWIFT; bank notifies Treasury Manager of document arrival (typically 5–10 days after shipment)
Responsible (R): Vendor / Bank
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Vendor-side</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1199_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1199_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1199_Task12" name="Document examination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Document examination: Treasury Manager and Import Coordinator examine shipping documents against LC terms within 5 banking days: (a) verify bill of lading (correct port, vessel, shipment date within LC window), (b) verify commercial invoice (amount within LC tolerance ±5%, correct PO reference), (c) verify packing list (quantities match PO), (d) verify certificate of origin, (e) flag discrepancies (late shipment, short shipment, document mismatch)
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1199_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1199_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1199_Task13" name="Discrepancy resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Discrepancy resolution: If discrepancies found in Step 5: (a) minor discrepancies (typo, formatting): Treasury Manager accepts and authorizes payment, (b) material discrepancies (wrong quantity, late shipment, missing document): Treasury Manager contacts Purchasing Manager to decide: (i) waive discrepancy and accept, (ii) request vendor to correct documents, or (iii) refuse documents and reject shipment; decision within 3 banking days to avoid bank refusal
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Purchasing Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1199_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1199_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1199_Task14" name="LC payment release">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: LC payment release: Upon document acceptance: bank debits BuildRight&#x27;s USD account and releases payment to vendor&#x27;s bank; system records payment: (a) DR: Accounts Payable — Import Vendor (USD), (b) CR: USD Bank Account, (c) FX gain/loss recorded if LC amount was hedged per W62 (FX management); AP Clerk reconciles payment against PO and goods receipt per 3-way match (W7)
Responsible (R): Bank / Treasury Manager / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1199_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1199_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1199_Task15" name="LC closure and cost accounting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: LC closure and cost accounting: After goods received and cleared customs (per W2B): system matches LC cost (bank fees, LC margin, amendment fees) to import PO; allocates landed cost components (product cost + freight + insurance + customs duty + bank charges) to inventory cost per WAC method; Treasury Manager tracks total LC costs for monthly treasury report
Responsible (R): System / Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min/LC</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1199_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1199_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1199_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1199_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1199_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-285 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Payment &amp; Reconciliation (PA-15.2).) | - operational: providing vendors with clear document requirements template and pre-shipment document review; operational: 5-banking-day document examination in Step 5 and pre-emptive discrepancy resolution; operational: FX hedging per W62
Owner: Treasury Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1199_Assoc18" sourceRef="W1199_Annotation17" targetRef="W1199_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1199_Flow19" sourceRef="W1199_Start7" targetRef="W1199_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1199_Flow20" sourceRef="W1199_Task8" targetRef="W1199_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1199_Flow21" sourceRef="W1199_Task9" targetRef="W1199_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1199_Flow22" sourceRef="W1199_Task10" targetRef="W1199_Task11" />
