    <bpmn:process id="W_W1310" name="W1310. Import Letter of Credit (LC) Lifecycle Management, Amendment &amp; Settlement Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Import purchase order requires LC payment per vendor agreement; or LC amendment requested by vendor; or LC maturity (payment due to bank)
Frequency: ~50–80 new LCs opened per month (for import vendors requiring LC terms); ~5–10 LC amendments per month
Volume: ~400–600 TEUs/month imported; ~40% of imports (by value) require LC payment; average LC value: PHP 2–5M per container shipment
Owner: Treasury Manager
Participants: Treasury Manager, Treasury Analyst, Import Coordinator, Category Manager, AP Clerk, Bank Trade Finance Officer
Source: workflow W1310 — Import Letter of Credit (LC) Lifecycle Management, Amendment &amp; Settlement Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1310_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1310_Lane1" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1310_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1310_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1310_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1310_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1310_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1310_Lane2" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1310_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1310_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1310_Start4" name="Import purchase order requires LC payment per vendor agreement; or LC amendment requested…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1310_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1310_Task5" name="LC application &amp; opening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: LC application &amp; opening: (a) when import PO is approved per W2B and vendor requires LC payment: Import Coordinator provides LC requirements to Treasury: (i) vendor name and bank details, (ii) LC amount (PO value + allowable tolerance ± 5–10%), (iii) LC type (sight or usance), (iv) required documents: commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificate of origin, insurance certificate, phytosanitary certificate (for wood products), (v) latest shipping date and document presentation deadline, (vi) shipping terms (FOB, CIF, CFR — per vendor agreement), (vii) port of discharge (Manila, Cebu, or Davao per DC allocation); (b) Treasury Analyst prepares LC application for issuing bank (BDO, BPI, or Chinabank — BuildRight maintains LC facilities with all three): (i) complete bank&#x27;s LC application form with all terms, (ii) attach supporting documents: approved PO, proforma invoice, vendor agreement; (c) Treasury Manager reviews and signs LC application; (d) submit to bank via trade finance portal or in-person; (e) bank opens LC and transmits SWIFT MT700 to vendor&#x27;s bank; (f) LC opening fee debited from BuildRight&#x27;s account (0.125–0.25% of LC value); (g) system records LC in treasury module: LC number, issuing bank, vendor, amount, terms, status = &quot;Open&quot;
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours per LC</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1310_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1310_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1310_Task6" name="LC document checking &amp; acceptance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: LC document checking &amp; acceptance: (a) when vendor ships goods: vendor&#x27;s bank presents shipping documents to BuildRight&#x27;s issuing bank; (b) bank notifies Treasury Analyst of document arrival; (c) Treasury Analyst and Import Coordinator review documents for compliance with LC terms: (i) commercial invoice: amount within LC tolerance, correct description, correct buyer; (ii) bill of lading: correct port of loading/discharge, correct consignee, on-board date before latest shipping date; (iii) packing list: quantities match invoice; (iv) certificate of origin: matches vendor country; (v) insurance certificate: covers CIF value if applicable; (d) if documents comply: Treasury Manager authorizes bank to accept documents and honor LC at maturity; (e) if documents have discrepancies: (i) common discrepancies: late shipment, partial shipment, invoice amount over LC tolerance, missing document, incorrect consignee; (ii) Import Coordinator contacts vendor to resolve — options: accept discrepancy (if minor), request amendment, or reject documents; (iii) for minor discrepancies (typo in description, slight quantity variance within tolerance): accept and pay; (iv) for major discrepancies (wrong goods, amount significantly over LC): reject documents, demand corrected documents or LC amendment
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours per document set</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1310_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1310_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1310_Task7" name="LC amendment processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: LC amendment processing: When LC terms need to change post-opening: (a) common amendments: (i) extend latest shipping date (vendor production delay), (ii) increase LC amount (PO quantity increased or price adjustment from exchange rate fluctuation), (iii) change port of discharge (vessel routing change); (b) Import Coordinator requests amendment from Category Manager with justification; (c) Treasury Manager approves amendment; (d) Treasury Analyst submits amendment application to bank; (e) bank issues amendment via SWIFT MT707 to vendor&#x27;s bank; (f) amendment fee (PHP 2,000–5,000) debited from BuildRight&#x27;s account; (g) system updates LC record with amended terms
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours per amendment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1310_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1310_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1310_Task8" name="LC settlement &amp; payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: LC settlement &amp; payment: (a) for sight LC: upon document acceptance (step 2d), bank debits BuildRight&#x27;s account immediately for LC amount + bank charges; (b) for usance LC: bank debits BuildRight&#x27;s account at maturity (e.g., 60 days after document acceptance); (c) Treasury Analyst reconciles bank debit: (i) LC amount matches PO value (within tolerance), (ii) bank charges match expected fee schedule, (iii) FX rate applied by bank matches BSP rate on value date (for USD-denominated LCs); (d) system records payment: (i) debit AP vendor account (clear import PO payable), (ii) debit bank charges expense, (iii) credit bank account; (e) for USD LCs: Treasury Analyst checks FX rate — if bank applied unfavorable rate, dispute with bank&#x27;s trade finance desk; (f) system updates LC status to &quot;Settled&quot;
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per settlement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1310_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1310_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1310_Task9" name="Monthly LC portfolio reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly LC portfolio reporting: (a) Treasury Manager compiles monthly LC portfolio report: (i) total open LCs by vendor and value, (ii) total LCs settled in the month, (iii) upcoming LC maturities (next 30/60/90 days) — cash flow planning for import payments, (iv) total bank charges by bank, (v) LC amendment frequency and cost (high amendment rate may indicate PO accuracy issues), (vi) discrepancy rate (high rate indicates vendor document quality issues or LC term mismatches); (b) report to CFO for cash flow planning and bank relationship management
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1310_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1310_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1310_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1310_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1310_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-285 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Payment &amp; Reconciliation (PA-15.2).) | - operational: Treasury Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Treasury Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1310_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1310_Annotation11" targetRef="W1310_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1310_Flow13" sourceRef="W1310_Start4" targetRef="W1310_Task5" />
